I am really surprised that this game has mixed reviews. It has it problems, but it's definitely a good game (at least at the current moment).
If you are interested in joining Magic players at PC you have only 2 ways: Magic 2014 Gold Complete (with incredible modding community to keep up with the actual current releases if you are interested) and Magic Duels (if you prefer to stay with something official and more classic with boosters and free deck builder). And I totally can say that Magic Duels is great not only as introduction to MTG, but as game on its own.
* You can pay for boosters (like in real Magic) or farm with daily quests or story mode;
* AI is actually quite good, I'm still impressed with its baiting and planning skills (it seems as improved version from 2014-2015 Magics);
* Good deck builder;
* Fair prices for boosters with both real money or in-game currency;
* Fine UI;
* Fine matchmaking with real people;
* Always incredible MTG inside.
I don't know why not to love this game. Also developers still working on improvements to the game and hear the community. Not always, but at least Magic Duels definitely improves over time.
From the downsides for newcomers, I can note the fact that second main phase should be always stopped with timer in order to play your cards, because game doesn't wait for your decision about them at second main phase. It's not a big deal, but a bit hard to newcomers and frustrating if you were lost in thoughts and forgot to stop manually.
Overall, I'm posting this review to say that this game worth more than "mixed" review at its current stage and I would recommend Duels along with Magic 2014 Gold for anyone who interested in Magic The Gathering. Magic Duels for PvP, current releases and better deck building and Magic 2014 for everyone who wants more casual experience (cards are limited for each deck), more “friendly” AI and PvE (hard to find opponent in Magic 2014).

