Having played the original and beaten this, here's what the entire game boils down to:
- Find yourself in an area, move about while killing groups of enemies until you find a button/switch that needs to be pressed to open a door, lift a crane, or toggle power to a piece of machinery;
- Destroy 1-3 waves of enemies so that said switch becomes "operable" and press it;
- Get presented with a few seconds of story dialogue, move to another area, repeat.
Boss fights are: evade attacks of the invincible boss while killing random adds, shoot one of the "highlighed/weakened" body parts of the boss, repeat 5+ times.
Positive:
1. Dececent graphics and smooth performance;
2. About 20min of comic book-like cutscenes between missions to support the story;
3. Fast-paced action.
Negative:
1. Linear level design, levels look like they offer more freedom than they actually do;
2. Oversized weapon models and mostly uninspired weapons (weapon modifications);
3. Unrewarding secrets that do not really offer anything except adding a bit more ingame currency to buy weapon modifications (unless i missed some easter-eggs);
4. Poor variety of enemies;
5. Relatively easy boss fights, usually preceeded by more difficult waves of stronger regular enemies.

The game is a buggy mess as expected and is normal in an EA game;
However, they dev's keep making questionable design decisions that make the game pretty much unplayable.
I suspect this will end up being more abandonware in the end, so for now you are probably better of holding onto your money.
